{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+ & Gram-, Antifungal", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "Unknown", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (40.54%) to Styelin D K:30%; V: 16%;G: 14%. GRAVY: -0.86; Mol Wt: 4349.204; Mol formula: C210H330N56O43; mol ex coeff: 23690. Activity: Active against B. clausii (MIC 3.1 ug/ml), S. epidermidis ATCC 700565 (MIC 3.1 ug/ml), E. coli O4 (MIC 50 ug/ml), P. mirabilis ATCC 29906 (MIC 6.3 ug/ml), and S. cerevisiae (MIC 6.3 ug/ml). Lower MBC of 12.5 ug/ml was found for S. epidermidis and S. cerevisiae, indicating a bactericidal effect. Antimicrobial robustness: Thermal stability: MIC 6.3 ug/mL against S. epidermidis after heating for 15 min at 100oC. More active at a basic pH than acidic pH (pH-sensitive). (salt-insensitive) MIC remained the same under physiological 150 mM NaCl, although it increased with an increase in salt concentrations from 300 mM to 600 mM. MOA: the peptide has an effect on cell morphology. Jan2023.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Mar. Drugs 2023; 21:74. https:// doi.org/10.3390/md21020074. MDPI", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03579", "source_id": "AP03579", "source_numeric_id": "03579", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03579", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Botryllin, a Novel Antimicrobial Peptide from the Colonial Ascidian Botryllus schlosseri", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
